    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d446">

                <pb facs="0610" n="602" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg602"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/11–1641</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Draft Prepared in the Division of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi><anchor n="28" xml:id="d446-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1941-11-16">November 16, 1941</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Outline of an Agreement</hi>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) That Japan shall forthwith desist from
                        any and all offensive military operations: offensive military operations to
                        mean launching of new offensive movements in <hi rendition="#italic">any
                            area</hi> and enlargement of Japanese <pb facs="0611" n="603"
                            xml:id="pg603"/> military establishments at <hi rendition="#italic">any
                            points</hi> outside of Japanese territory (among such areas and points
                        being Manchuria, China, Indochina, Thailand, Malaya and insular areas not
                        under Japanese sovereignty or mandate).</item>
                    <label/>
                    <item>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) That the United States shall within six
                        months relax its embargoes upon trade with Japan.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>That the two countries shall within six months rescind, reciprocally,
                        their respective freezing regulations and operations, each so far as the
                        other is concerned.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>(A provision for economic policy—on the lines of the draft of such a
                        provision given to Admiral Nomura on November 15<anchor n="29"
                            xml:id="d446-f2"/>).</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>That in case Japan embarks upon any further offensive military operations
                        the obligations of the United States under this agreement shall
                        automatically terminate.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
